 "about_text": "La Luz de Jesus Gallery is a Los Angeles gallery founded in 1986 by entrepreneur and art collector Billy Shire. Housed inside the Soap Plant/Wacko complex on Hollywood Boulevard, the gallery is credited with helping foster what became known as the Lowbrow or Pop Surrealist movement in California art. Its program favors figurative, narrative painting and unconventional sculpture, with content spanning folk, outsider, religious, and sexually charged themes. The gallery states its mission is to bring underground art and counter-culture to a wider audience, and it also operates an Art Advisor Service connecting collectors, curators, and designers with contemporary artists worldwide.",
